(6352665, 939799, 73115, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by giantmike:</b></div><hr/><i> I like how your lighting. It''s either the sun rising over the horizon, or a great simulation of that event.<br/>What is the coffee alternative? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, there was a table lamp, sort of a Tiffany style, as the light source and my coffee alternative is hot chocolate.  I can''t stand the taste of coffee so I figured if I was going to pay for something I would get something I liked :)<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the votes and comments everyone!</td>', 'Originally posted by giantmike: I like how your lighting. It''s either the sun rising over the horizon, or a great simulation of that event.What is the coffee alternative?   Actually, there was a table lamp, sort of a Tiffany style, as the light source and my coffee alternative is hot chocolate.  I can''t stand the taste of coffee so I figured if I was going to pay for something I would get something I liked :) Thanks for all the votes and comments everyone!', '2011-03-16 01:15:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6352694, 939810, 128304, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by uskesu:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice work on the coffee explosion. But the rest of the picture I don''t particularly like. What''s those balckish things in the background? Why this cup? And does a splash really make better coffee? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you.<br/>the tins are just that coffee, sugar and tea tins. I was actualy in that kind of mood i picked this cup randomly, the splash was just me trying to learn some technics, i have a lot of practice to go but it is way way fun :) and no it was just some cold instant coffee lol.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by uskesu: Nice work on the coffee explosion. But the rest of the picture I don''t particularly like. What''s those balckish things in the background? Why this cup? And does a splash really make better coffee?   Thank you.the tins are just that coffee, sugar and tea tins. I was actualy in that kind of mood i picked this cup randomly, the splash was just me trying to learn some technics, i have a lot of practice to go but it is way way fun :) and no it was just some cold instant coffee lol.', '2011-03-16 01:46:32.000000', NULL, 0),
